$$\text{Period } T = \frac{1}{20\text{ kHz}} = 50\text{ }\mu\text{s}$$

With a 170 MHz clock ($T_{\text{tick}} \approx 5.882\text{ ns}$):
$$\text{Total ticks} = \frac{170,000,000\text{ Hz}}{20,000\text{ Hz}} = 8500\text{ ticks}$$

Choosing prescaler $\text{PSC} = 0$, the Auto-Reload Register value is:
$$\text{ARR} = 8500 - 1 = 8499$$

For a 25% active-high duty cycle in PWM Mode 1:
$$\text{CCR1} = 8500 \times 0.25 - 1 = 2124 \implies 2125\text{ ticks}$$

